From 3a7a800318f1909a94dfad7cc85d21e11653c929 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 10:42:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 07/31] a210: vendor import: 55-optional-peripherals

Cherry-picked vendor enablement group 55 (55-optional-peripherals) onto Linux v6.6.141 as
the maintained A210 LTS branch (one commit per kernel/patches group). Applied
with git apply --recount; reconciled against vendor branch osl/a210-v2.9.0.
See kernel/patches/README.md and kernel/T2-DESIGN.md for group rationale.

Signed-off-by: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>

v7.0 port adaptations (optional peripherals):
- cpufreq/pwm/usb-dwc3/virtio Kconfig+Makefile: union-merged the vendor
  configs (xuantie/zhihe cpufreq, pwm-thead, dwc3-thead/-zhihe, vdmabuf)
  alongside the new upstream ones.
- iio/adc, pci-dwc, virtio_ids: added only the vendor entries, de-duped the
  symbols upstream already carries.
- pci/pcie-designware.h: kept upstream\x27s LTSSM/atu_phys_addr additions; the
  vendor pcie-zh register #defines applied cleanly and pcie-zh.c depends on
  them.
- rtc/rtc-xgene: kept the vendor xgene_rtc_set_prescaler() call (A210 RTC is
  snps,dw-apb-rtc, bound here) but upstream\x27s device_init_wakeup(...,true).
- usb/dwc2/params: re-added dwc2_set_zhihe_params (its match entry is in the
  same file) next to upstream\x27s new ltq danube/ase functions.
- usb/dwc3/core: kept the vendor usb_speed/usb_mode module-param overrides and
  upstream\x27s new num_hc_interrupters default.
- perf/riscv_pmu_sbi: took upstream (the vendor delta was a 32-bit-only path,
  dead on the rv64 A210).
- spi-dw: kept reg_map_size in the header (spi-dw-mmio.c uses it) but took
  upstream spi-dw-core.c, dropping the vendor quad-SPI 32-bit DMA dfs quirk.
  SPI is off the boot/install path; revisit if quad-SPI flash misbehaves.

Signed-off-by: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
